Because running VSLAM is fun (1.0) 📷🧭📍

Last Monday I had the opportunity to run some experiments at the #QUT Space Technology Precinct (Yandiwanba) at the QUT (Queensland University of Technology) (Kelvin Grove campus).

📽 Video: https://lnkd.in/gB9afryj

🌙 Yandiwanba is a lunar simulation lab designed to evaluate planetary rover missions in realistic conditions, equipped with space robotics hardware and advanced sensing systems. The name Yandiwanba (Yan-dee-wan-ba) comes from the Yagarabul language and means “to go from below to above,” or “from the ground to a higher place, way above.” 

During the session I collected a dataset using a #GoPro and quickly generated: camera calibration and  a reference trajectory using structure-from-motion with #GLOMAP.

I then ran our latest system, AllFeature-VSLAM, which tightly couples multiple types of features (ORB and ALIKED in this case).

The dataset and experiments are fully reproducible using #VSLAMLAB with a single command: 

pixi run demo allfeature-dev videos GX010216

